message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Interpretable Multi-Task Fusion Framework for Wind Farm Siting"
date-released: 2026-09-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-org>/interpretable-wind-siting-multitask"
keywords:
  - wind energy
  - site selection
  - deep learning
  - TabTransformer
  - BERT-LoRA
  - cross-modal learning
  - multi-task learning
  - GradNorm
  - SHAP
  - explainable AI
  - policy NLP
abstract: > "Companion repository for the manuscript 'An Interpretable
  Multi-Task Fusion Framework for Wind Farm Siting Combining Policy
  Semantics and Meteorological Features'. Implements a cross-modal
  architecture that fuses TabTransformer on 16 spatial features,
  Chinese-BERT+LoRA on policy text, and 4-head cross-modal attention,
  balanced by GradNorm across three task heads, with SHAP-based
  interpretability. Validated against nine SCADA-confirmed sites in China."